an College and entered MIT graduate study."}, {"year": 1966, "age": 24, "event": "Proposed the working-set model for program behavior while on Project MAC."}, {"year": 1968, "age": 26, "event": "Published the working-set CACM paper (ACM Best Paper) and completed MIT PhD."}, {"year": 1973, "age": 31, "event": "Published classic textbook Operating Systems Theory with Ed Coffman."}, {"year": 1981, "age": 39, "event": "Helped found CSNET, a key bridge from ARPANET toward the broader Internet."}, {"year": 1983, "age": 41, "event": "Founded RIACS at NASA Ames as an interdisciplinary computational-science center."}, {"year": 2002, "age": 60, "event": "Joined Naval Postgraduate School, later chairing CS and leading innovation institutes."}], "total_leverage_score": 15, "inherited_access_stack_count": 6, "exceptional_inherited_access_count": 2, "all_documented_early_condition_count": 6}
